
i want to walk through a queue of people.
and see if removing up to one person
can make them line up according to their heights.

i pick the first person.
compare them to the next.

if i find they're taller than the next.
    that's an imbalance.
    i can't forgive that.

    i note it.
    now, i go to the third number.
    the question becomes.

    who owns this third number?
    the first or the second.

    well, whoever fits.

    if the first person fits.
    then that's the streak i want to continue.

    if the second person fits.
    continue instead.

    what if they both fit?
    how would that work.

    fit would mean the third number is taller than them both.
    well, yes.

    you could have 5, 3, 8
    in which case, would it matter?
    you can only numbers 8 or more moving on.

    so again, the third number goes with the first one that fits.
    and what if it doesn't fit?

    then you stop it.
    it would seem, i'm on to something.

    you start iterating at the second number.
    compare it to the one before it,
    and the one before the one before it.

    every number should follow one of them.
    at ths start, you'd only have one number to follow.

    if it doesn't follow. you'd have an imbalance.
    so note it.

    on the next iteration, now you're at the third number.
    this number must follow one of the two before it.
    if not, another imbalance, and there you go.

    i think this approach works much better.